// PEAR 2 rejects a `letrec` group whose initializer is not a lambda.
//
// Recursion is lowered by lifting each member to a module-level function; an
// arbitrary initializer has no lifted definition to call, so the group is not
// expressible without a fixpoint over stored values, which the backend does not
// model. The group is refused with a positioned diagnostic naming the rule.
air 2.2 Main "reject_letrec_non_lambda_main.pie";

def main() : i64 =
  mu~ %ret.
    letrec (answer = 42 : i64) in
      <answer | %ret>;
